Left out: about 10 seconds switching slides, and a remark about the time.

11:15.426 --> 11:39.963
On the issue of agency and agent stochasticity: we've mentioned that LLMs can have a great degree of agency. You don't know exactly what you're going to get, and initially you may start with most of the behavior encoded in LLM inference, just a markdown file maybe.

11:39.963 --> 11:56.538
As you work more on your problem, you may build a small deterministic layer where you have a tool and the agent starts calling that tool. You've reduced the amount of inference and encoded some behavior in a more testable way, maybe with unit tests or other things.

11:56.538 --> 12:09.589
Then you may go further right and have a thinner agent layer, and maybe workflows: different tools that serve each other, with the agent either orchestrating them or being part of them.

12:09.589 --> 12:32.230
You may even go to an extreme where you remove inference completely. That last case is what we do most: we have AI all around it, but maybe we end up with a very well-known problem, and that removes inference. Use inference where it matters, and engineer it away where it doesn't.

12:32.230 --> 12:51.259
The takeaways, which we've already had spoilers for: Qualify the capabilities that you need, not the model. It doesn't matter how an agent is implemented; it only matters whether it's good enough for you. And on the subject of good enough: make that good enough executable.

12:51.259 --> 13:06.057
A little goes a long way towards being able to trust the AI systems you use. Finally, use these exams to build, not just to score.

13:06.057 --> 13:25.974
You can use it as test-driven development of sorts, or eval-driven development, and an important point is around the word evals. Don't just think, "I'll run something and get 66% accuracy." It's a fuzzy number. It means nothing. No one knows what to do with it.

13:25.974 --> 13:36.192
Make it pass/fail, make it yes/no, and own that gating. Then you'll be able to delegate heavily to these agents.

13:36.192 --> 13:51.820
If I have to give you advice: start with one behavior your AI must get right, turn it into an exam, and make any implementation pass it. Thank you very much.
